<h1>Gatherings</h1>
<p>
  Eight seats, and he has opinions about all of them. There is no
  calendar. When something is planned it will be on this page, and
  when it isn't, nothing is.
</p>

<article class="card">
  <h2 class="card__title">Cats (2019), with cake and tea</h2>
  <p class="card__meta">
    A Saturday in October, date to be confirmed &mdash; the lounge
  </p>
  <p>
    He does not watch films. He insisted on this one. It is a horror
    picture if you are a cat: people become cats, and nobody asks
    them. There will be cake, which is for the club, and tea, which is
    for you. You are a guest of the club, and these are different
    things.
  </p>
  <p class="u-muted">
    Capacity eight. Leaving early is permitted, but noted.
  </p>
</article>

<article class="card">
  <h2 class="card__title">Halloween</h2>
  <p class="card__meta">
    <time datetime="2026-10-31">Saturday 31 October</time> &mdash;
    after dark
  </p>
  <p>
    He is running the game. Character sheets are printed and on the
    table, and he has filled in his own. Something dark is on in the
    background, and nobody has been told what the chronicle is about.
    Costumes are optional. He will be wearing his own.
  </p>
  <p class="u-muted">
    See <a href="/vampire/">his sheet</a>. Capacity eight.
  </p>
</article>

<p>
  Matters of importance, or of nobility, go to
  <a href="mailto:themooncat@eml.cc">him</a>. Everything else goes to
  <a href="mailto:kirsten@eml.cc">the Familiar</a>, who passes things
  on.
</p>

<blockquote class="saying">
  <p class="saying__text">Wait long enough and the lap arrives.</p>
